      "description": "Assistant Professor - Accounting (Reopened) FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT The Business Department of Queensborough Community College is seeking applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor faculty position in the field of accounting. We are interested in candidates who have professional or teaching experience in the field of accounting. Reporting to the Department Chairperson, the candidate will perform teaching and research in areas of expertise and share responsibilities for committee and department assignments, performing administrative, supervisory and other functions as may be assigned. CUNY is an equal opportunity employer, is committed to increasing the diversity of its workforce and is dedicated to recruiting and retaining professionals who share the College’s commitment to equity. It welcomes nominations of, and applications from members of protected groups including minorities, women, veterans and individuals with disabilities, as well as others who would bring additional perspectives to the university’s mission. Candidates with demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusiveness through their research, teaching and/or service are also encouraged to apply. One of Queensborough Community College’s greatest strengths, and a necessary element of excellence, is the diversity of our community. We strive to attract and nurture a talented and diverse faculty and staff that proudly reflect the unique character of the local Queens community, the most diverse county in the United States. As a community college in the CUNY system, our diverse student population primarily take general education and lower division courses often for university transfer. Contractual teaching load is 24 contact hours for the academic year, summer optional. Faculty on Assistant Professor tenure track receive reassigned time to pursue scholarship. For additional information please visit https://www.qcc.cuny.edu/business/index.html QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. degree or equivalent from a regionally accredited college/university in Accounting or related field or a Master’s Degree in Accounting or related field or MBA from a regionally accredited college/university in accounting or taxation andaCPA. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS MBA Demonstrated professional business accounting experience in the field. Prior undergraduate teaching experience (in-person, hybrid, or fully online) in a broad range of accounting courses including Principles of Accounting, Intermediate Accounting, Taxes, Cost Accounting, and Computerized Accounting. Experience with curriculum development, program assessment, service on committees. Experience with Learning Management Platforms (LMS) such as Brightspace teaching in various modalities. Experience teaching a diverse student population. A record of recent publications and/or scholarly research and grants. COMPENSATION Salary $84,011 - $91,922. Commensurate with experience and qualifications. Please refer to https://psc-cuny.org/issues/contract-apeoplescuny/ta-2023-2027/salary-schedules/ for the PSC-CUNY recently ratified salary schedules reflecting the 2023-2027 contract. CUNY offers faculty competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must provide a CV/resume and cover letter. CLOSING DATE SEARCH REOPENED Open Until Filled. Previous Applicants need not reapply. JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 30665 Location: Queensborough CC Job Type: Full-Time",
